course: dictionary
lesson: 13949
title: Liable: responsible or likely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Liable is a formal word with three main meanings. Liable for something means you are responsible for it, often by law: «The club is liable for injuries on its land.» It means the club may have to pay.
explain: Liable to means likely to happen, usually something bad: «That old shelf is liable to fall.» The shelf has not fallen yet, but the danger is real. Liable to can also mean likely to get something, such as a fine: «Drivers are liable to a fine for parking here.»
explain: Look at the words around liable to find its meaning. If the sentence is about who must pay or take the blame, it means responsible. If it is about what might happen, it means likely. Then test your meaning in the sentence: if "responsible for" or "likely to" fits, you have it.
fact: Liable has three meanings: responsible by law, likely to happen, and likely to get something or be affected by it.
fact: «Liable for» means responsible, as in «liable for damage».
fact: «Liable to» means likely to, as in «liable to fall».
fact: «Held liable» means a person has been found responsible, for example after an accident.
fact: You will mostly find liable in rules, signs and formal notices.
exercise: «The shop is not liable for lost coats left at the door.» What does liable for mean here? | *Responsible, so it does not have to pay | Happy to keep coats safe | Very fond of coats | Likely to lose coats
exercise: «The old bridge is liable to collapse in a storm.» What does liable to mean here? | Brand new and strong | Certain to be painted soon | *Likely to happen, usually something bad | Able to swim across
exercise: «Drivers are liable to a fine for parking here.» What might a driver get? | A prize | A cup of tea | *A fine | A new car
test: «The club is liable for injuries on its land.» Here, liable for means | Very tired after a match | Likely to go to sleep | Happy about the land | *Responsible for paying for harm
test: Ella says liable means funny. Which meaning fits «The ice is liable to melt in the sun»? | Hard to see | Very cold | Funny to watch | *Likely to melt
exam: «The driver was held liable for the crash.» What does held liable mean? | *Found responsible for the crash | Glad to be in a car | Given a free ride home | Very sleepy after the drive
